            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse perforated necrotising amoebic colitis with histoplasmosis in an immunocompetent individual presenting as an acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-009059</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013009059</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Perforated necrotising amoebic colitis associated with intestinal histoplasmosis has rarely been reported in an immunocompetent individual. Radiology and preoperative features are non-specific and requires histopathological examination for a definitive diagnosis. Hence, this condition needs to be considered in the differential diagnosis of complicated infective colitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
